      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 505,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 544,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70567,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 160,
        "headingId": 544,
        "headingText": "<p>Paratestis or testis</p>",
        "timestamp": "2022-04-15T17:41:16"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 506,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 545,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70568,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 160,
        "headingId": 545,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Serous cystadenomas are usually cystic tumours. They may cause symptoms related to mass effects, or they may be incidental findings.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T15:29:00"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 507,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 546,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70569,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 160,
        "headingId": 546,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These are rare tumours. Patient ages range from 35&nbsp;to 73&nbsp;years.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T15:29:00"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 508,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 547,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70570,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 160,
        "headingId": 547,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Ovarian-type epithelial tumours of the testis are believed to originate from remnants of M&uuml;llerian ducts in paratesticular connective tissue, epididymis, and spermatic cord, or from M&uuml;llerian metaplasia of the mesothelium of the tunica vaginalis of the testis {28543997}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T15:29:00"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 509,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 548,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70571,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 160,
        "headingId": 548,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T15:29:00"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 516,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 555,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70572,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 160,
        "headingId": 555,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The cut surface of the testis shows circumscribed cystic lesions about 35&nbsp;mm in size {32619438}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T15:29:00"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 510,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 549,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70573,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 160,
        "headingId": 549,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Tumours are cystic and contain serous fluid. The cysts are lined by a non-stratified cuboidal to ciliated columnar epithelium with abundant pale cytoplasm and bland nuclei {32619438}.</p>\r\n<p>Immunohistochemically, the tumour cells are positive for pancytokeratin, WT1, PAX8, ER, PR, and CK7, and they are negative for OCT3/4 and calretinin. Ki-67 expression is low {28543997}.</p>\r\n<p>The differential diagnosis is with reactive mesothelial hyperplasia.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T15:29:00"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 511,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 550,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70574,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 160,
        "headingId": 550,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>No published data</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T15:29:00"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 512,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 551,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70575,
